  ],
  "notes": "Root failure mode is a latent design/configuration error (megawatt transducer circuit LDA setpoint incorrect for full-power operation), which was only revealed when a weather-induced electrical fault produced a turbine speed transient that crossed the erroneous 1809 RPM setpoint. Both the external fault and the misconfiguration are modeled as parallel inputs converging on LDA actuation, per rule 5 (single trigger with two causal inputs). No previous occurrences (Section G) or applicable backups stated in narrative; RCS/turbine valve systems and 500kV bus are modeled as directly involved per the event description, not as design-context-only mentions."
